  <main id="main-content" role="main" class="poster">
    <header class="animate">
      <div class="topbar">
        <div>
          <div class="venue">IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy</div>
          <div class="case">Case: science.org / DOI 10.1126/science.add1585 / CDN edge verification</div>
        </div>
        <div class="badge">Academic publishing security</div>
      </div>
      <section class="hero" aria-label="Poster title and thesis">
        <div>
          <h1 class="hero-title">Bot Mitigation at Scale</h1>
          <p class="subtitle">How modern CDN-based web security services protect high-value scientific publishing platforms from scraping, credential abuse, and bot-surge availability threats.</p>
        </div>
        <article class="card claim">
          <div class="claim-label">Central finding</div>
          <p class="claim-text">Challenge-based verification pipelines dramatically reduce automated scraping while preserving near-perfect uptime and low friction for legitimate researchers.</p>
        </article>
      </section>
    </header>

    <section class="metric-strip animate delay-1" aria-label="Five key metrics">
      <article class="card metric-card feature">
        <div class="metric-value" data-count="85" data-suffix="%">85%</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Reduction in unauthorized bulk scraping attempts after deployment</div>
      </article>
      <article class="card metric-card feature-green">
        <div class="metric-value" data-count="99.97" data-suffix="%">99.97%</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Uptime maintained during bot surge events exceeding 10× normal traffic</div>
      </article>
      <article class="card metric-card">
        <div class="metric-value" data-count="47" data-prefix="~" data-suffix="%">~47%</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Estimated share of 2024 internet traffic originating from bots</div>
      </article>
      <article class="card metric-card">
        <div class="metric-value" data-count="30" data-suffix="%">30%</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Share of bot traffic classified as malicious</div>
      </article>
      <article class="card metric-card">
        <div class="metric-value">&lt;2s</div>
        <div class="metric-label">Typical end-to-end challenge latency for legitimate users</div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <div class="layout">
      <div class="left-stack">
        <section class="card" data-reveal aria-labelledby="threat-title">
          <div class="section-eyebrow">01 / Threat landscape</div>
          <h2 id="threat-title" class="section-title">Academic content is a high-value automation target.</h2>
          <p class="body-copy">Scientific publishers host peer-reviewed articles, supplementary datasets, and DOI-linked assets. High traffic and valuable intellectual property create incentives for large-scale scraping, credential stuffing, and denial-of-service automation.</p>
          <div class="threat-grid">
            <div class="mini-stat"><strong>1.2M</strong><span>Scraping attempts per day before mitigation</span></div>
            <div class="mini-stat"><strong>78%</strong><span>Average origin CPU load before CDN enforcement</span></div>
            <div class="mini-stat"><strong>10×</strong><span>Observed bot surge intensity over normal traffic</span></div>
            <div class="mini-stat"><strong>Ray ID</strong><span>Traceable edge identifiers enable incident forensics</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="trafficChart" role="img" aria-label="Doughnut chart showing 47 percent bot traffic and 53 percent human traffic"></canvas></div>
        </section>

        <section class="card" data-reveal aria-labelledby="outcomes-title">
          <div class="section-eyebrow">03 / Outcomes</div>
          <h2 id="outcomes-title" class="section-title">Security gains without availability loss.</h2>
          <div class="outcomes">
            <div class="outcome-list">
              <div class="delta"><div class="delta-num">−85%</div><p>Unauthorized scraping declined from ~1.2M to ~180K attempts per day.</p></div>
              <div class="delta"><div class="delta-num">−46%</div><p>Average origin CPU load fell from 78% to 42% after edge filtering.</p></div>
              <div class="delta"><div class="delta-num">−72%</div><p>Monthly legitimate-user complaints fell from 1,200 to 340.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="chart-wrap"><canvas id="outcomeChart" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart comparing before and after mitigation outcomes"></canvas></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="comparison-title">Before → after mitigation profile</div>
          <div class="bars" aria-label="Comparison bars">
            <div class="bar-row"><span>Scraping/day</span><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width: 15%"></div></div><span>180K</span></div>
            <div class="bar-row"><span>Origin CPU</span><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width: 54%"></div></div><span>42%</span></div>
            <div class="bar-row"><span>Uptime surge</span><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width: 99.97%"></div></div><span>99.97%</span></div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="right-stack">
        <section class="card pipeline" data-reveal aria-labelledby="pipeline-title">
          <div class="section-eyebrow">02 / Technical mechanism</div>
          <h2 id="pipeline-title" class="section-title">Challenge-Based Verification Pipeline</h2>
          <p class="body-copy">Requests are intercepted at the CDN edge, scored using reputation and fingerprinting signals, challenged when risk exceeds threshold, validated, and forwarded with a session token only after verification.</p>
          <div class="flow" aria-label="Sequential verification pipeline">
            <article class="step"><div class="step-num">1</div><h3>Request interception</h3><p>Incoming HTTP request routes through the nearest CDN edge node before origin contact.</p><span class="duration">&lt;50 ms</span></article>
            <article class="step"><div class="step-num">2</div><h3>Threat scoring</h3><p>IP reputation, TLS fingerprint, and behavioral signals are evaluated for automation risk.</p><span class="duration">~100 ms</span></article>
            <article class="step"><div class="step-num">3</div><h3>Challenge issuance</h3><p>High-risk sessions receive JavaScript or CAPTCHA challenges before content access.</p><span class="duration">~500 ms</span></article>
            <article class="step"><div class="step-num">4</div><h3>Verification check</h3><p>Client response is validated and assigned a traceable Ray ID for monitoring.</p><span class="duration">~200 ms</span></article>
            <article class="step"><div class="step-num">5</div><h3>Access grant</h3><p>Verified users reach the publisher origin with a valid session token.</p><span class="duration">&lt;50 ms</span></article>
          </div>
          <div class="latency-callout"><strong>&lt;150 ms</strong><span>Average page-load overhead for already-verified sessions; total human challenge completion typically remains under 2 seconds.</span></div>
        </section>

        <section class="card" data-reveal aria-labelledby="trade-title">
          <div class="section-eyebrow">04 / Usability vs. security</div>
          <h2 id="trade-title" class="section-title">Trade-offs make the system research-relevant, not merely operational.</h2>
          <p class="body-copy">The core design challenge is balancing bot resistance with seamless access for researchers, educators, and institutional subscribers.</p>
          <div class="trade-grid">
            <article class="trade"><div class="trade-icon">♿</div><h3>Accessibility</h3><p>Challenge pages must satisfy WCAG 2.1 to avoid excluding users with disabilities.</p></article>
            <article class="trade"><div class="trade-icon">🏛️</div><h3>Institutional access</h3><p>University IP ranges can be allowlisted to reduce unnecessary campus challenges.</p></article>
            <article class="trade"><div class="trade-icon">🔎</div><h3>Transparency</h3><p>Clear “security verification” messaging explains short delays and reduces confusion.</p></article>
            <article class="trade"><div class="trade-icon">🛡️</div><h3>Privacy</h3><p>Threat detection must disclose data practices and minimize unnecessary collection.</p></article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="card" data-reveal aria-labelledby="takeaways-title">
          <div class="section-eyebrow">05 / Takeaways</div>
          <h2 id="takeaways-title" class="section-title">Operational telemetry enables continuous optimization.</h2>
          <div class="takeaways">
            <article class="takeaway"><p>Bot traffic represents nearly half of requests to internet-scale publisher websites.</p></article>
            <article class="takeaway"><p>CDN-edge verification blocks most malicious automation before origin impact.</p></article>
            <article class="takeaway"><p>Trace identifiers such as <span class="ray">9edb9b44499904f9</span> support forensic analysis.</p></article>
            <article class="takeaway"><p>Publisher–CDN collaboration sustains open, secure access to scientific knowledge.</p></article>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
    <footer class="footer">
