          <div class="comparison-title">Before → after mitigation profile</div>
          <div class="bars" aria-label="Comparison bars">
            <div class="bar-row"><span>Scraping/day</span><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width: 15%"></div></div><span>180K</span></div>
            <div class="bar-row"><span>Origin CPU</span><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width: 54%"></div></div><span>42%</span></div>
            <div class="bar-row"><span>Uptime surge</span><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width: 99.97%"></div></div><span>99.97%</span></div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="right-stack">
        <section class="card pipeline" data-reveal aria-labelledby="pipeline-title">
          <div class="section-eyebrow">02 / Technical mechanism</div>
          <h2 id="pipeline-title" class="section-title">Challenge-Based Verification Pipeline</h2>
          <p class="body-copy">Requests are intercepted at the CDN edge, scored using reputation and fingerprinting signals, challenged when risk exceeds threshold, validated, and forwarded with a session token only after verification.</p>
          <div class="flow" aria-label="Sequential verification pipeline">
            <article class="step"><div class="step-num">1</div><h3>Request interception</h3><p>Incoming HTTP request routes through the nearest CDN edge node before origin contact.</p><span class="duration">&lt;50 ms</span></article>
            <article class="step"><div class="step-num">2</div><h3>Threat scoring</h3><p>IP reputation, TLS fingerprint, and behavioral signals are evaluated for automation risk.</p><span class="duration">~100 ms</span></article>
            <article class="step"><div class="step-num">3</div><h3>Challenge issuance</h3><p>High-risk sessions receive JavaScript or CAPTCHA challenges before content access.</p><span class="duration">~500 ms</span></article>
            <article class="step"><div class="step-num">4</div><h3>Verification check</h3><p>Client response is validated and assigned a traceable Ray ID for monitoring.</p><span class="duration">~200 ms</span></article>
            <article class="step"><div class="step-num">5</div><h3>Access grant</h3><p>Verified users reach the publisher origin with a valid session token.</p><span class="duration">&lt;50 ms</span></article>
          </div>
          <div class="latency-callout"><strong>&lt;150 ms</strong><span>Average page-load overhead for already-verified sessions; total human challenge completion typically remains under 2 seconds.</span></div>
        </section>

        <section class="card" data-reveal aria-labelledby="trade-title">
          <div class="section-eyebrow">04 / Usability vs. security</div>
          <h2 id="trade-title" class="section-title">Trade-offs make the system research-relevant, not merely operational.</h2>
          <p class="body-copy">The core design challenge is balancing bot resistance with seamless access for researchers, educators, and institutional subscribers.</p>
